{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array formed by repeating\n    the given array's first n elements k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input validation (equivalent to Validator class logic)\n    if not arr:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array cannot be empty.\")\n    if not (0 < n <= len(arr)):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid value for n. n must be > 0 and <= len(arr) ({len(arr)}), but got {n}.\")\n    if not (k > 0):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid value for k. k must be > 0, but got {k}.\")\n\n    # Select the first n elements (equivalent to SelectedSegment)\n    selected_segment = arr[:n]\n\n    # Construct the repeated array by concatenating the segment k times (equivalent to RepeatedArray)\n    # This explicit construction adheres to the design's current implementation choice.\n    repeated_array_elements = selected_segment * k\n\n    # Apply Kadane's Algorithm to find the maximum contiguous subarray sum\n    # (equivalent to KadaneAlgorithm.computeMaxSubarray)\n    # This version correctly handles arrays with all negative numbers by returning the largest single element.\n    if not repeated_array_elements:\n        # This case should ideally not be reached if n > 0 and k > 0 are validated,\n        # as selected_segment will not be empty, thus repeated_array_elements will not be empty.\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = repeated_array_elements[0]\n    current_max = repeated_array_elements[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(repeated_array_elements)):\n        current_max = max(repeated_array_elements[i], current_max + repeated_array_elements[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "def get_Inv_Count(array) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts inversions in an array using a brute-force approach.\n    An inversion exists for indices (i, j) if i < j and array[i] > array[j].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    inversion_count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                inversion_count += 1\n    return inversion_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/293", "solution": "import math\nfrom numbers import Real\ndef compute_hypotenuse(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle using the Pythagorean theorem.\n    Returns the result as a float.\n    \"\"\"\n    return math.sqrt(a**2 + b**2)\ndef otherside_rightangle(a, b) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the third side (hypotenuse) of a right-angled triangle.\n    Requires both input parameters to be numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    validate_parameters(a, b)\n    return compute_hypotenuse(a, b)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/294", "solution": "def max_val(list_input):\n    \"\"\"Compute maximum numeric value in list_input, ignoring non-numeric elements.\n    Raises ValueError if no numeric elements are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    numeric_values = []\n    for value in list_input:\n        if isinstance(value, (int, float)) and not isinstance(value, bool):\n            numeric_values.append(value)\n\n    if not numeric_values:\n        raise ValueError(\"No numeric elements found in list_input (behavior per design decision).\")\n\n    return max(numeric_values)"}
