{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits of each number in a list, then sums these individual sums.\n    Negative numbers are treated by their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum_of_all_digits = 0\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        # Use absolute value for negative numbers.\n        current_num = abs(number)\n        current_digit_sum = 0\n\n        # Calculate sum of digits for the current number.\n        # Handle 0 explicitly to avoid entering the loop for 0.\n        if current_num == 0:\n            current_digit_sum = 0\n        else:\n            while current_num > 0:\n                digit = current_num % 10\n                current_digit_sum += digit\n                current_num //= 10\n        \n        total_sum_of_all_digits += current_digit_sum\n        \n    return total_sum_of_all_digits"}
