{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "class Pair:\n    \"\"\"Represents a pair of integers and provides methods for its product and ordered tuple.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, a: int, b: int) -> None:\n        self.a = a\n        self.b = b\n\n    def product(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the product of the two integers in the pair.\"\"\"\n        return self.a * self.b\n\n    def ordered_tuple(self) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the pair as a tuple (smaller, larger).\"\"\"\n        return (min(self.a, self.b), max(self.a, self.b))\ndef _compute_candidate_pairs(nums: list[int]) -> list[Pair]:\n    \"\"\"Generates all unique unordered pairs from the input list.\"\"\"\n    candidate_pairs = []\n    n = len(nums)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            candidate_pairs.append(Pair(nums[i], nums[j]))\n    return candidate_pairs\ndef _select_max_pair(pairs: list[Pair]) -> Pair:\n    \"\"\"Selects the pair with the maximal product, applying tie-breaking rule BR9.\"\"\"\n    # This case is implicitly handled by validate_input ensuring len >= 2,\n    # leading to at least one pair.\n    max_pair = pairs[0]\n    max_product = max_pair.product()\n\n    for i in range(1, len(pairs)):\n        current_pair = pairs[i]\n        current_product = current_pair.product()\n\n        if current_product > max_product:\n            max_product = current_product\n            max_pair = current_pair\n        elif current_product == max_product:\n            # Apply deterministic tie-break BR9:\n            # prefer pair whose larger element is greatest;\n            # if still tied, prefer pair whose smaller element is greatest.\n            current_a, current_b = current_pair.ordered_tuple()\n            max_a, max_b = max_pair.ordered_tuple()\n\n            if current_b > max_b:\n                max_pair = current_pair\n            elif current_b == max_b and current_a > max_a:\n                max_pair = current_pair\n    return max_pair\ndef max_Product(nums: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair with the highest product from a given array of integers.\n    The returned tuple is ordered (smaller, larger).\n    \"\"\"\n    validate_input(nums)\n    candidate_pairs = _compute_candidate_pairs(nums)\n    selected_pair = _select_max_pair(candidate_pairs)\n    return selected_pair.ordered_tuple()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/418", "solution": "def Find_Max(items: list) -> object:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element of a list having the maximum length.\n    Returns the first element encountered with the maximal length in case of a tie.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        raise ValueError(\"Find_Max: input list is empty\")\n\n    max_len = -1\n    selected_item = None\n\n    for item in items:\n        current_len = len(item)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            selected_item = item\n\n    return selected_item"}
